---
// Privacy policy of the personal "hermes-agent" Google OAuth app (linked from the Google Cloud consent screen,
// so keep the URL stable). English only: Google reviews it.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

export const prerender = false;

const updated = 'October 27, 2026';
---

<Layout locale="en" title="Privacy policy" description="How the personal Hermes assistant uses Google account data." alternates={false}>
  <section class="container head">
    <h1 class="h1">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="label muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container body">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This page describes how "hermes-agent", a personal AI assistant run by Syafwan Iqbal Fauzi on his own server, uses Google
        account data. The app is for personal use. It is not offered to the public, and the only accounts connected to it belong to
        its owner.
      </p>

      <h2>What the app accesses</h2>
      <p>
        When the owner connects one of his own Google accounts, the app asks for access to Gmail (read, send and modify), Google
        Calendar, Google Drive, Google Contacts (read only), Google Sheets and Google Docs. It uses this access only to carry out
        tasks the owner asks for, such as reading and labelling email, checking the calendar, or updating a spreadsheet.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>OAuth tokens that keep the connection working are stored on the owner's private server, readable only by the owner. They are never published and never shown on any web page.</li>
        <li>The owner's private dashboard stores only the account address, a label, the connection status, the list of granted permissions and the time of the last check.</li>
        <li>Email, calendar, file and contact content is read when a task needs it. It is not copied into a database for other purposes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How data is used and shared</h2>
      <p>
        Data from Google accounts is used only to provide the assistant's features to the owner. It is not sold, not used for
        advertising, and not shared with anyone else. To carry out a task, the relevant content may be sent to the AI model
        provider the assistant runs on (currently Anthropic), solely to produce the result the owner asked for.
      </p>
      <p>
        The use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Removing access</h2>
      <p>
        Access can be withdrawn at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
        Once access is withdrawn the stored token stops working, and it can be deleted from the server on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: see the contact details on the <a href="/en/about">about page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-15);
    padding-block: var(--s-66) var(--s-33);
  }

  .body {
    padding-bottom: var(--s-66);
    max-width: 760px;
  }
</style>
